{ "answer": ["Albumin"], "clues": ["Approximately 25% of people who are allergic to cats or dogs are actually reacting to this substance, rather than the animal's fur. Rarely, some highly cat-allergic individuals can actually experience severe allergic reactions when eating pork, a bizarre cross-reactivity known as Pork-Cat syndrome","As the US prepared to enter World War II, the military wanted to develop a stable, compact blood substitute to treat battlefield shock and burns. Because this substance is found in most vertebrates, scientists initially believed human and bovine versions of this substance were identical enough and began clinical trials on inmates at Norfolk State Prison Colony and Harvard Medical Students. This triggered severe, delayed serum sickness and the bovine military program was permanently shut down.","Providing approximately 80% of the colloid osmotic pressure in blood vessels, this protein folds into a distinct heart-shaped conformation"] },
